sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A1 as Admin 1: POST /floors/:id/rooms
  participant DB as Postgres
  participant A2 as Admin 2: POST /floors/:id/rooms

  Note over A1,A2: Free plan (limit 3), org currently has 2 active rooms
  A1->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT ... FROM organizations JOIN plans WHERE id = org FOR UPDATE OF o
  DB-->>A1: row lock granted, room_limit = 3
  A2->>DB: BEGIN, SELECT ... FOR UPDATE OF o
  Note right of DB: Admin 2 WAITS on the org row lock
  A1->>DB: SELECT count(*) FROM rooms WHERE is_active → 2
  A1->>DB: 2 < 3 → INSERT rooms
  A1->>DB: COMMIT (lock released)
  DB-->>A2: lock granted
  A2->>DB: SELECT count(*) → 3 (sees Admin 1's room)
  A2->>A2: 3 ≥ 3 → throw 402 PLAN_LIMIT_REACHED
  A2->>DB: ROLLBACK
  Note over A1,A2: Test: 6 simultaneous creates at 2/3 → exactly one 201, five 402s
  Note over A1,A2: Same lock also guards reactivating a room, and serializes with the Stripe webhook's plan change (an UPDATE of the same row)
